{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Remember the days of old.</b> He says: give heart to remember, from the time of creation, the good that He did with you at the time of formation — this is what it says, ״בהנחיל עליון גוים״ (when the Most High gave the nations their inheritance)." "<b>Understand the years of generation and generation.</b> That is, they should understand what was done in the generations from the hour the Shekhinah dwelt among them — this is what it says, ״ימצאהו בארץ מדבר״ (He found him in a desert land). And the word יצב is a root-noun (מקור), like להציב (to set/establish), and likewise (Jeremiah 1) ״לא דעתי דבר״ — 'I did not know' (as infinitive). And the meaning of the verse will be: when the Holy One, blessed be He, gave the nations their inheritance and separated them into their tongues, in the manner written in the genealogies of those who came forth from Noah (Genesis 10:32), ״ומאלה נפרדו הגוים״ — 'and from these the nations were separated' — you will find in that passage of genealogies seventy persons, to allude to the seventy nations destined to come forth from them. And therefore the verse explains that when the Holy One, blessed be He, separated the tongues, to establish ״גבולות עמים״ — 'the borders of the peoples' — which are seventy, למספר בני ישראל יורדי מצרים (according to the number of the children of Israel who went down to Egypt), who were seventy souls, He chose none other than Israel, whom He set apart as His portion — this is ״כי חלק ה׳ עמו״ (for HaShem's portion is His people). And there are those who interpreted ״גבולות עמים״ (the borders of the peoples) as the diagonals of the world, which are twelve, over which are appointed twelve constellations, corresponding to the number of the children of Israel — that is, the twelve tribes of Israel; and immediately after it comes the verse ״כי חלק ה׳ עמו״ — 'for HaShem's portion is His people' — not the portion of the stars and constellations. And in this verse it is explicitly stated that Israel is not under the governance of the stars and constellations, but they are above them; and this supremacy no other nation attained, ״ולא עשה כן לכל גוי״ — 'and He did not do so for any nation.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The citation '(ירמיה א)' is apparently meant for Jeremiah 1:6 (לא דעתי דבר); the abbreviation resolved by context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:10.307453061Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}